athWorksDocPage/Example" itemprop="example" class="em_example"><meta itemprop="exampleid" content="stats-ex96600123"></meta><meta itemprop="exampletitle" content="Feature Selection Using kFold Edges"></meta></div></div></div><div class="ref_sect"><h2 id="mw_48a58084-23d0-4c26-8e88-220b9b3b3c4c">Input Arguments</h2><div class="expandableContent"><p class="switch "><a href="javascript:void(0);" class="expandAllLink" data-allexpanded="true">collapse all</a></p><div class="panel-group" id="mw_48a58084-23d0-4c26-8e88-220b9b3b3c4c_panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel panel-default "><div itemscope="" itemprop="inputargument" itemtype="http://www.mathworks.com/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/NamedInputArgument" itemid="mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_mw_8402f6a9-15e3-4a71-8bee-ca559d4957a7"><div role="tab" data-toggle="collapse" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_mw_8402f6a9-15e3-4a71-8bee-ca559d4957a7" data-target="#expand_panel_body_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_mw_8402f6a9-15e3-4a71-8bee-ca559d4957a7" aria-controls="expand_panel_body_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_mw_8402f6a9-15e3-4a71-8bee-ca559d4957a7" class="panel-heading add_cursor_pointer" aria-expanded="true"><span id="inputarg_CVMdl" class="anchor_target"></span><h3 class="panel-title" id="mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_mw_8402f6a9-15e3-4a71-8bee-ca559d4957a7"><code itemprop="name">CVMdl</code> &#8212; <span itemprop="purpose">Cross-validated, binary kernel classification model</span><br/> <span class="add_font_color_general remove_bold"><span class="example_desc"><span itemprop="inputvalue"><code class="literal">ClassificationPartitionedKernel</code> model object</span></span></span></h3><span class="icon-arrow-open-down icon_24"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right icon_24"></span></div><div role="tabpanel" id="expand_panel_body_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_mw_8402f6a9-15e3-4a71-8bee-ca559d4957a7" aria-labelledby="expand_panel_heading_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_mw_8402f6a9-15e3-4a71-8bee-ca559d4957a7" class="panel-collapse collapse in"><div class="panel-body"><p>Cross-validated, binary kernel classification model, specified as a <a href="classreg.learning.partition.classificationpartitionedkernel.html"><code class="object">ClassificationPartitionedKernel</code></a> model object. You can create a
                <code class="object">ClassificationPartitionedKernel</code> model by using <a href="fitckernel.html"><code class="function">fitckernel</code></a>
            and specifying any one of the cross-validation name-value pair arguments.</p>
        <p>To obtain estimates, <code class="literal">kfoldEdge</code> applies the same data used to
            cross-validate the kernel classification model (<code class="literal">X</code> and
                <code class="literal">Y</code>).</p></div></div></div></div></div><span id="namevaluepairarguments" class="anchor_target"></span><span id="mw_5fab342b-3e34-4223-b97b-abfd3037e6c4" class="anchor_target"></span><h3 id="namevaluepairs" class="bottom_ruled">Name-Value Pair Arguments</h3><div class="namevaluecontainer"><p class="nvpair_boilerplate">Specify optional
      comma-separated pairs of <code class="argument">Name,Value</code> arguments. <code class="literal">Name</code> is
      the argument name and <code class="literal">Value</code> is the corresponding value.
        <code class="literal">Name</code> must appear inside quotes. You can specify several name and value
      pair arguments in any order as <code class="literal">Name1,Value1,...,NameN,ValueN</code>.</p><span class="example_desc"><strong>Example: </strong><code class="literal">kfoldEdge(CVMdl,'Mode','individual')</code> returns the
        classification edge for each fold.</span></div><div class="ref_sect"><div class="expandableContent"><div class="panel-group" id="mw_9d6bea41-9fe3-41c5-9313-90d633782199_panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel panel-default "><div itemscope="" itemprop="inputargument" itemtype="http://www.mathworks.com/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/NameValuePairInputArgument" itemid="mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Folds"><div role="tab" data-toggle="collapse" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Folds" data-target="#expand_panel_body_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Folds" aria-controls="expand_panel_body_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Folds" class="panel-heading add_cursor_pointer" aria-expanded="true"><span id="inputarg_Folds" class="anchor_target"></span><h3 class="panel-title" id="mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Folds"><code itemprop="name">'Folds'</code> &#8212; <span itemprop="purpose">Fold indices for prediction</span><br/> <span class="add_font_color_general remove_bold"><span class="example_desc"><span itemprop="inputvalue defaultvalue"><code class="literal">1:CVMdl.KFold</code></span> (default) | <span itemprop="inputvalue">numeric vector of positive integers</span></span></span></h3><span class="icon-arrow-open-down icon_24"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right icon_24"></span></div><div role="tabpanel" id="expand_panel_body_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Folds" aria-labelledby="expand_panel_heading_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Folds" class="panel-collapse collapse in"><div class="panel-body">
<p>Fold indices for prediction, specified as the comma-separated pair consisting of
                <code class="literal">'Folds'</code> and a numeric vector of positive integers. The elements
            of <code class="argument">Folds</code> must be within the range from <code class="literal">1</code> to
                <code class="literal">CVMdl.KFold</code>.</p>
<p>The software uses only the folds specified in <code class="argument">Folds</code> for
            prediction.</p>
<p class="description_valueexample"><strong>Example: </strong><code class="literal">'Folds',[1 4 10]</code></p>
<p class="datatypelist"><strong>Data Types: </strong><code itemprop="datatype">single</code> | <code itemprop="datatype">double</code></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel panel-default "><div itemscope="" itemprop="inputargument" itemtype="http://www.mathworks.com/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/NameValuePairInputArgument" itemid="mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Mode"><div role="tab" data-toggle="collapse" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Mode" data-target="#expand_panel_body_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Mode" aria-controls="expand_panel_body_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Mode" class="panel-heading add_cursor_pointer" aria-expanded="true"><span id="inputarg_Mode" class="anchor_target"></span><h3 class="panel-title" id="mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Mode"><code itemprop="name">'Mode'</code> &#8212; <span itemprop="purpose">Aggregation level for output</span><br/> <span class="add_font_color_general remove_bold"><span class="example_desc"><span itemprop="inputvalue defaultvalue"><code class="literal">'average'</code></span> (default) | <span itemprop="inputvalue"><code class="literal">'individual'</code></span></span></span></h3><span class="icon-arrow-open-down icon_24"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right icon_24"></span></div><div role="tabpanel" id="expand_panel_body_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Mode" aria-labelledby="expand_panel_heading_mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Mode" class="panel-collapse collapse in"><div class="panel-body">
    <p>Aggregation level for the output, specified as the comma-separated pair consisting of
        <code class="literal">'Mode'</code> and <code class="literal">'average'</code> or
        <code class="literal">'individual'</code>.</p>
    <p>This table describes the values.</p>
<div class="table-responsive"><table class="table table-condensed"><colgroup><col class="tcol1" width="50%"></col><col class="tcol2" width="50%"></col></colgroup><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code class="literal">'average'</code></td><td>The output is a scalar average over all folds.</td></tr><tr><td><code class="literal">'individual'</code></td><td>The output is a vector of length <em class="varname">k</em> containing one value per
                fold, where <em class="varname">k</em> is the number of folds.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>
</p>
    <p class="description_valueexample"><strong>Example: </strong><code class="literal">'Mode','individual'</code></p>
  </div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="ref_sect"><h2 id="mw_42f2242e-ee5b-468a-ad39-4340d1c5e757">Output Arguments</h2><div class="expandableContent"><p class="switch "><a href="javascript:void(0);" class="expandAllLink" data-allexpanded="true">collapse all</a></p><div class="panel-group" id="mw_42f2242e-ee5b-468a-ad39-4340d1c5e757_panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel panel-default "><div role="tab" data-toggle="collapse" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_f8e4c598-5445-4a0d-bbcc-44982b91c6ea" data-target="#expand_panel_body_mw_f8e4c598-5445-4a0d-bbcc-44982b91c6ea" aria-controls="expand_panel_body_mw_f8e4c598-5445-4a0d-bbcc-44982b91c6ea" class="panel-heading add_cursor_pointer" aria-expanded="true"><span id="outputarg_edge" class="anchor_target"></span><h3 class="panel-title" id="mw_f8e4c598-5445-4a0d-bbcc-44982b91c6ea"><code class="name">edge</code> &#8212; Classification edge<br/> <span class="add_font_color_general remove_bold"><span class="example_desc">numeric scalar | numeric column vector</span></span></h3><span class="icon-arrow-open-down icon_24"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right icon_24"></span></div><div role="tabpanel" id="expand_panel_body_mw_f8e4c598-5445-4a0d-bbcc-44982b91c6ea" aria-labelledby="expand_panel_heading_mw_f8e4c598-5445-4a0d-bbcc-44982b91c6ea" class="panel-collapse collapse in"><div class="panel-body">
          <p><a href="classreg.learning.partition.classificationpartitionedkernel.kfoldedge.html#mw_59b05187-79f6-4400-aff2-4867ce3498cd" class="intrnllnk">Classification
              edge</a>, returned as a numeric scalar or numeric column vector.</p>
          <p>If <a href="#mw_b0f72f1d-d42b-4a18-af69-f0e90d3fe555_sep_shared-Mode" class="intrnllnk"><code class="argument">Mode</code></a> is <code class="literal">'average'</code>, then
              <code class="argument">edge</code> is the average classification edge over all folds.
            Otherwise, <code class="argument">edge</code> is a <em class="varname">k</em>-by-1 numeric column
            vector containing the classification edge for each fold, where <em class="varname">k</em> is
            the number of folds.</p>
        </div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="moreabout ref_sect"><h2 id="mw_ea3d56fd-aa30-40bb-9ca4-d5eebd3239c6">More About</h2><div class="expandableContent"><p class="switch"><a href="javascript:void(0);" class="expandAllLink" data-allexpanded="true2">collapse all</a></p><div class="expand_collapse"><h3 class="expand_trigger" id="mw_59b05187-79f6-4400-aff2-4867ce3498cd" aria-expanded="true" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#expand_body_mw_59b05187-79f6-4400-aff2-4867ce3498cd" aria-controls="expand_body_mw_59b05187-79f6-4400-aff2-4867ce3498cd"><span class="icon-arrow-open-down"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right"></span>Classification Edge</h3><div id="expand_body_mw_59b05187-79f6-4400-aff2-4867ce3498cd" class="collapsible_content collapse in" aria-expanded="true"><p class="shortdesc">The <em class="firstterm">classification edge</em> is
the weighted mean of the <em class="firstterm">classification margins</em>.</p><p>One way to choose among multiple classifiers, for example to perform feature selection, is to
                choose the classifier that yields the greatest edge.</p></div></div><div class="expand_collapse"><h3 class="expand_trigger" id="mw_f446add7-1782-46d3-9780-53e45a3dd23b" aria-expanded="true" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#expand_body_mw_f446add7-1782-46d3-9780-53e45a3dd23b" aria-controls="expand_body_mw_f446add7-1782-46d3-9780-53e45a3dd23b"><span class="icon-arrow-open-down"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right"></span>Classification Margin</h3><div id="expand_body_mw_f446add7-1782-46d3-9780-53e45a3dd23b" class="collapsible_content collapse in" aria-expanded="true"><p class="shortdesc">The <em class="firstterm">classification margin</em> for binary classification
        is, for each observation, the difference between the classification score for the true class
        and the classification score for the false class.</p><p>The software defines the classification margin for binary classification as</p>
<div id="d120e410200" class="mediaobject"><div class="code_responsive"><p class="programlistingindent"><!--MathType@Translator@5@5@MathML2(Clipboard).tdl@MathML2.0(Clipboard)@--><math altimg='eqn1448907927.png' altimg-valign='-8px' display='block' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML'><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow></math><!--MathType@End@5@5@--></p></div></div><p><em class="varname">x</em> is an observation. If the true label of
            <em class="varname">x</em> is the positive class, then <em class="varname">y</em> is 1, and &#8211;1
        otherwise. <em class="varname">f</em>(<em class="varname">x</em>) is the positive-class classification
        score for the observation <em class="varname">x</em>. The classification margin is commonly
        defined as <span class="inlineequation"><em class="varname">m</em> =
                    <em class="varname">y</em><em class="varname">f</em>(<em class="varname">x</em>)</span>.</p><p>If the margins are on the same sca